      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Proceeding from the results obtained by the analysis of laparotomies performed in the year 1972 and 1973 in all gynaecological and surgical hospital departments of the city Brno, the authors conclude, that the most cases of pathological haemorrhages of corpus luteum or Graaf's follicul --82,8 per cent -- were not received and operated at the gynaecological clinics, but at the surgical departments. The paper is analysing how much this fact can be caused by diagnostic mistakes. That disparity is apparently also able to impress the common false presumption in the gynaecology, that those haemorrhages are constituting only a very rare and curious case."},
